            <div xml:id="d384">

                <pb facs="0465" n="353" sameAs="frus:frus1918/pg353"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 837.61351/83a</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the United States Food Administrator</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Hoover</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-01-14">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 14, 1918</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The Department of State has received,
                    under date of January 11, an informal inquiry from your office as to whether the
                    official approval of the Department would be given to the preliminary and
                    confidential copy of the agreement which it was understood was entered into
                    between the International Sugar Committee of the United States Food
                    Administration, the Cuban commission, the Cuban committee for arranging
                    commercial terms appointed by the President of the Republic of Cuba, agents of
                    various Cuban producers acting severally for the producers of sugar in the
                    island of Cuba, and the Royal commission on the sugar supply, and refiners of
                    sugar in the United States.</p>
                <p>In reply to the above inquiry I wish to inform you that, in view of the fact
                    that, pursuant to your request, the Cuban Minister was informed on November 8
                    that, respecting the price for Cuban sugar, it appeared that the matter was one
                    for determination between buyers and sellers with as little Government
                    intervention as possible, this Department can not see its way clear to make any
                    statement in regard to the agreement in question.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Frank L. Polk</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
